roken engineering and more about beginning to build the guardrails that would let AI contributions be trusted at all.","strengths":["A disciplined, high-signal test suite (99 assertions across 3 files, 0.60 test-to-source ratio) exercises every input permutation plus a dedicated compatibility suite ported from the `classnames` library","GitHub Actions CI runs on every push/PR across a 6-version Node matrix, builds the distributable bundles, and reports coverage to Codecov","Conventional-commit discipline (73%) and a fast, small-batch merge cadence (median 7.8h to merge) reflect a lean, well-maintained solo workflow","A clear, example-rich README documents every usage pattern and all three distribution formats, giving strong human onboarding even without agent-specific docs"],"risks":["Zero machine-readable AI/agent guidance exists anywhere (D1=0), so any assistant working in this repo has no documented conventions, build/test commands, or constraints to anchor to — every AI session starts from scratch","Master is unprotected and 0% of sampled merged PRs carry a recorded review — nothing structurally distinguishes a reviewed change from an unreviewed one, human- or AI-authored","No dependency-update automation, SAST, or secret scanning exists at all, and none of the 3 Action references are pinned — the supply-chain surface is effectively unmonitored","No release automation or signed/provenance-tracked releases — version bumps appear to be manual commits, leaving no auditable, reversible path to publish that an agent could safely drive","D4 and D8 both sit at 0 — there is no scaffolding yet (review bots, evals, prompt library) to build AI trust on top of, so any AI adoption here would currently be entirely ad hoc"],"roadmap":[{"title":"Agent guidance is absent — an assistant dropped into this repo has nothing written down to work from","dimension":"D1","impact":"high","effort":"low","rationale":"Without a CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md, every AI session has to rediscover the bui